From a9be68952d70fdf602d188edafa4f2efa64a0ec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mitzev <ogi@kunasystems.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 23:22:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.45: rust-analyzer parser support for the `class` keyword
 (1.02 #1 Phase 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Teaches rust-analyzer to accept the rustcc fork's `class` keyword
as a weak contextual keyword. Classes parse cleanly as a new
CLASS syntax node (with CLASS_MEMBER_LIST child) instead of
producing the cascading ERROR nodes stock RA emitted, so LSP
features on surrounding items (hover / rename / go-to-def /
completion) continue to work in class-containing files.

Phase 1 scope — parser-level only:
- Adds `class` to CONTEXTUAL_KEYWORDS in the grammar codegen
  source, producing CLASS_KW + `[class]` macro.
- Adds `Class = Attr* Visibility? 'class' Name GenericParamList?
  (':' base:Type)? WhereClause? ClassMemberList` and
  `ClassMemberList = '{' fields:RecordField* methods:AssocItem* '}'`
  to `rust.ungram`. Regenerated `generated/nodes.rs` +
  `syntax_kind/generated.rs`.
- Teaches `items::opt_item_without_modifiers` to route
  `class IDENT` at item position to a new `adt::klass` parser.
- `adt::klass` parses the header (generics, optional `: BaseType`,
  where clause) and delegates the body to a new
  `class_member_list` that alternates record-field parsing and
  `item_or_macro` based on a `looks_like_field_at` peek.

Non-exhaustive match arms updated in downstream crates:
- `hir-expand/builtin/derive_macro.rs`: two sites (one treats
  class body as unit shape for derive, one walks class member
  list for path discovery).
- `hir/semantics/source_to_def.rs`: returns None for Adt::Class
  (no item-tree entry in Phase 1).
- `hir-def/item_tree/lower.rs`: returns None for Item::Class
  (Phase 2 will synthesize Struct + Impl items here).
- `ide-assists`: 9 sites updated — code-generation assists
  (gen_clone/debug/default/hash/partial_eq/partial_ord) bail on
  classes like they bail on unions; `extract_module` collects
  class fields from the member list; `add_lifetime_to_type`
  skips classes; the shared `utils.rs` descends into the member
  list for trait-where-clause inference.
- `syntax/ast/node_ext.rs`: `Adt -> Item` conversion routes
  Adt::Class to Item::Class.

Intentional non-coverage (Phase 2 work):
- Class items produce no item-tree entry, so hover / go-to-def
  targeting the class *name* don't resolve yet, and workspace
  symbol search doesn't surface classes. Everything else —
  including items INSIDE the class body and code AFTER it —
  works as if the class were a parse-visible block.

Validation:
- `cargo test -p parser` → 315/0 (was 314/0; +1 inline test)
- `cargo test -p syntax` → 51/0
- Manual probe: `echo 'pub class Widget { ... }' | rust-analyzer parse`
  now emits CLASS@<span> + CLASS_MEMBER_LIST children with zero
  error nodes. Generics and single-inheritance headers also
  round-trip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
